window.READING_LOGIC_MODULE_CONTENT = Object.freeze({"2":{"title":"具體資訊 → 上位概念","english":"Conceptual Abstraction","short":"具體 → 概念","phases":["基礎分類與初步抽象","語境、能力與共同概念","合理抽象與過度概括","多層資訊與綜合判斷"],"stages":[{"name":"先掌握核心想法","accent":"gold","steps":["<strong>原文常給一件具體的事</strong>，答案則用較大的概念概括它。","<blockquote>runs every morning → exercises every morning</blockquote><p>running 是 exercise 的一種；人物與時間仍要相同。</p>","<strong>抽象要有邊界：</strong>吃一次水果，可以說吃了 fruit；不能因此斷定這個人永遠健康。"]},{"name":"先理解什麼叫「具體」","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>例如：</p><blockquote>Amy can cook by herself.</blockquote><p>這句告訴我們一件很清楚的事情：</p><p>• 人：Amy • 行為：cook • 情況：by herself</p><p>它描述的是一個<strong>具體能力</strong>。</p><p>再看：</p><blockquote>Amy is more independent.</blockquote><p>這句沒有說她做哪一件事。</p><p>它把前面的具體能力放進一個較大的概念：</p><blockquote>independent</blockquote><blockquote><strong>cook by herself → greater independence</strong></blockquote><p>前面的具體資訊，可以支持後面的較大概念。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Ben runs every morning. 哪句較一般的描述有根據？","options":[{"label":"Ben exercises every morning.","correct":true,"feedback":"對！running 是 exercise 的一種，時間也保持一致。"},{"label":"Ben wins every race.","correct":false,"feedback":"跑步不代表贏得每一場比賽。"}]}},{"name":"最基本的形式：自己做事 → 更獨立","accent":"blue","steps":["<p>這是最容易理解的一種。</p>","<h3>Example 1</h3><blockquote>Ben can walk to school by himself.</blockquote><p>可以推出：</p><blockquote>Ben is more independent.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p><strong>by himself</strong> 告訴我們：</p><blockquote>Ben 不需要另一個人陪他去。</blockquote><p>「可以自己完成事情」是 independence 的一個重要部分。</p><blockquote><strong>go to school by himself → more independent</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 2</h3><blockquote>Anna can make breakfast by herself.</blockquote><p>可以推出：</p><blockquote>Anna is more independent.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>具體資訊是：</p><blockquote>make breakfast by herself</blockquote><p>較大的概念是：</p><blockquote>independence</blockquote><p>她可以自己完成日常事情，所以這個具體能力可以支持：</p><blockquote>more independent</blockquote>","<h3>Example 3</h3><blockquote>Sam can take the bus by himself.</blockquote><p>可以推出：</p><blockquote>Sam is more independent.</blockquote>","<h3>邏輯</h3><p>具體：</p><blockquote>take the bus by himself</blockquote><p>上位概念：</p><blockquote>independent</blockquote><p>推理方向：</p><blockquote><strong>自己搭車 → 可以自己出行 → 更獨立</strong></blockquote><p>這裡已經有兩個很小的推理步驟。</p>"]},{"name":"同一個概念可以有很多具體例子","accent":"coral","steps":["<p>這一點很重要。</p><p>「independent」是一個比較大的概念。</p><p>很多不同的行為都可以放進去：</p><blockquote>cook by yourself travel by yourself shop by yourself clean your room by yourself go to school by yourself</blockquote><p>所以可以想成：</p><p>這就是：</p><blockquote><strong>小的具體行為 → 大的概念</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體行為 → safe","accent":"green","steps":["<blockquote>The dog helps John walk around cars.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>The dog helps John stay safe.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>具體行為：</p><blockquote>helps John walk around cars</blockquote><p>表示 John 可以避開危險。</p><p>較大的概念：</p><blockquote>safe</blockquote><blockquote><strong>avoid danger → stay safe</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體結果 → healthy","accent":"gold","steps":["<blockquote>Mia eats fruit and vegetables every day.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>Mia eats healthy food.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>fruit 和 vegetables 都是常見的 healthy food。</p><blockquote><strong>fruit + vegetables → healthy food</strong></blockquote><p>這裡的上位概念是：</p><blockquote>healthy food</blockquote><p>具體例子是：</p><blockquote>fruit vegetables</blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體行為 → helpful","accent":"blue","steps":["<blockquote>Jack carries his mother&#x27;s bags.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>Jack helps his mother.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>具體行為：</p><blockquote>carries her bags</blockquote><p>這是一種 help。</p><blockquote><strong>carry her bags → help her</strong></blockquote><p>這是一種很常見的閱讀題改寫。</p><p>文章給你：</p><blockquote>他做了什麼。</blockquote><p>答案給你：</p><blockquote>這個行為代表什麼。</blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體行為 → learning","accent":"coral","steps":["<blockquote>Lily reads English books every night.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>Lily studies English often.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>在這個語境中：</p><blockquote>reading English books</blockquote><p>可以是：</p><blockquote>studying English</blockquote><p>的一種方式。</p><blockquote><strong>read English books → study English</strong></blockquote><p>這裡學生要開始理解：</p><blockquote>一個較大的概念，可以包括很多不同做法。</blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體行為 → exercise","accent":"green","steps":["<blockquote>Tom runs for thirty minutes every morning.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>Tom exercises every morning.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>running 是 exercise 的一種。</p><blockquote><strong>run → exercise</strong></blockquote><p>這一種非常乾淨。</p><p>因為：</p><blockquote>run</blockquote><p>可以放在：</p><blockquote>exercise</blockquote><p>這個較大的概念裡。</p><p>例如 run、swim、walk 和 ride a bike 都是 exercise。</p><p>因此：</p><blockquote>Tom runs every morning.</blockquote><p>自然支持：</p><blockquote>Tom exercises every morning.</blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體交通方式 → travel","accent":"gold","steps":["<blockquote>Mary goes to work by bus.</blockquote><p>可以推出：</p><blockquote>Mary travels by bus.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><blockquote>go to work</blockquote><p>是一種移動。</p><p>所以它可以放進較大的概念：</p><blockquote>travel</blockquote><blockquote><strong>go from one place to another → travel</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體動作 → communication","accent":"blue","steps":["<blockquote>Ben calls his father every day.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>Ben talks with his father every day.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>calling someone 通常包括：</p><blockquote>talking with that person.</blockquote><blockquote><strong>call father → talk with father</strong></blockquote><p>這裡的答案比原文更一般。</p><p>原文告訴你<strong>怎樣談話</strong>：</p><blockquote>by phone</blockquote><p>答案只保留：</p><blockquote>talk</blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體地方 → outdoor activity","accent":"coral","steps":["<blockquote>Kate plays football in the park.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>Kate does an outdoor activity.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>具體資訊：</p><blockquote>plays football in the park</blockquote><p>較大的概念：</p><blockquote>outdoor activity</blockquote><p>足球在公園進行，所以這個活動可以被放進：</p><blockquote>outdoor activity</blockquote>"]},{"name":"具體行為 → care","accent":"green","steps":["<blockquote>Tom gives his dog food and water every day.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>Tom takes care of his dog.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><blockquote>give food give water</blockquote><p>都是：</p><blockquote>take care of a dog</blockquote><p>的一部分。</p><blockquote><strong>give food + water → take care of</strong></blockquote><p>這種題型在閱讀理解很常見。</p><p>文章寫很多小事情。</p><p>答案把它們放進一個大概念。</p>"]},{"name":"幾個具體行為一起支持一個概念","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>有時一個例子還不夠強。</p><p>文章可能給很多小資訊：</p><blockquote>Lisa cooks her own food.</blockquote><blockquote>She cleans her room.</blockquote><blockquote>She goes shopping by herself.</blockquote><p>題目：</p><blockquote>Lisa is independent.</blockquote><p>這時支持力很強。</p><p>因為 cook、clean 和 shop by herself 這三個具體行為，都指向同一個概念：</p><blockquote><strong>independent</strong></blockquote><p>這是一種：</p><blockquote><strong>多個具體資訊 → 一個共同概念</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"這裡要非常小心：不能看到一個例子就隨便放大","accent":"blue","steps":["<p>「具體 → 概念」需要有清楚的關係。</p><p>例如：</p><blockquote>Tom ate an apple.</blockquote><p>可以推出：</p><blockquote>Tom ate fruit.</blockquote><p>因為 <strong>apple → fruit</strong> 是清楚的包含關係。</p><p>但是：</p><blockquote>Tom ate an apple.</blockquote><p>不能直接推出：</p><blockquote>Tom is healthy.</blockquote><p>原因是：</p><blockquote>eat one apple</blockquote><p>只是一件事。</p><p>而：</p><blockquote>healthy</blockquote><p>是一個很大的狀態。</p><p>中間還缺很多資訊。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Tom ate one apple. 哪句有根據？","options":[{"label":"Tom ate fruit.","correct":true,"feedback":"對！apple 屬於 fruit。"},{"label":"Tom is healthy forever.","correct":false,"feedback":"一次吃蘋果不能證明永久健康。"}]}},{"name":"可以上推","accent":"coral","steps":["<blockquote>Jane drinks water every day.</blockquote><p>可以推出：</p><blockquote>Jane drinks something every day.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>water 是：</p><blockquote>something you can drink</blockquote><p>所以「喝水」必然也是「喝了某種東西」。這個關係很直接。</p>"]},{"name":"不可以推得太遠","accent":"green","steps":["<blockquote>Jane drinks water every day.</blockquote><p>不能直接推出：</p><blockquote>Jane is very healthy.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>「喝水」和「健康」有關係。</p><p>但一個人的健康還會受到很多事情影響。</p><p>所以 <strong>drink water</strong> 只能提供部分資訊，不能保證 <strong>very healthy</strong>。這是學生一定要學會的界線。</p>"]},{"name":"所以「具體 → 概念」有兩種強度","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>我們可以把它分成兩級。</p>","<h3>Level 1：很強的包含關係</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>run → exercise apple → fruit bus → transport cook by yourself → do something by yourself</blockquote><p>這些關係很穩。</p>","<h3>Level 2：語境支持的較大概念</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>travel by yourself → more independent avoid cars and people → travel safely give food and water to a dog → take care of the dog</blockquote><p>這些需要看整個句子的意思。</p><p>所以閱讀題裡，學生要問：</p><blockquote><strong>這個較大的概念，真的能被原文的具體資訊支持嗎？</strong></blockquote>","<h3>補充例子：獨立能力</h3><blockquote>need less help</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>more independent</blockquote><p>例如：</p><blockquote>Amy can cook without help.</blockquote><blockquote>Amy is more independent when she cooks.</blockquote><p>另一個例子：</p><blockquote>Ben can take the bus without help.</blockquote><blockquote>Ben is more independent when he travels.</blockquote>"]},{"name":"它和「全體 → 個體」的方向剛好很有意思","accent":"blue","steps":["<p>上一個概念：</p><blockquote><strong>全體 → 個體</strong></blockquote><p>例子：</p><blockquote>all fruit → mango</blockquote><p>它從大範圍走到小成員。</p><p>現在這個概念：</p><blockquote><strong>具體 → 上位概念</strong></blockquote><p>例子：</p><blockquote>run → exercise</blockquote><p>它從小例子走向較大的概念。</p><p>所以兩者看起來方向相反：</p>","<h3>全體 → 個體</h3><blockquote>FRUIT ↓ MANGO</blockquote><p>討論一句話對多少成員成立。</p>","<h3>具體 → 上位概念</h3><blockquote>RUN ↓ EXERCISE</blockquote><p>但兩者處理的東西不同。</p><p>第一個談：</p><blockquote><strong>一句話對多少成員成立</strong></blockquote><p>第二個談：</p><blockquote><strong>一個行為屬於什麼概念</strong></blockquote><p>這兩種推理處理的問題不同。</p>"]},{"name":"四步解題程序","accent":"coral","steps":["<p>解題時可以依照四步。</p>","<h3>Step 1：找具體資訊</h3><p>文章到底說了什麼？</p><p>例如：</p><blockquote>Ben goes shopping by himself.</blockquote>","<h3>Step 2：找答案中的大概念</h3><p>答案可能寫：</p><blockquote>Ben is more independent.</blockquote>","<h3>Step 3：問「這個行為是不是這個概念的一個例子？」</h3><p>如果答案很清楚，是，就繼續。例如 <strong>shop by himself → more independent</strong>。</p>","<h3>Step 4：檢查有沒有推得太遠</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>Ben shops by himself.</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>Ben is more independent.</blockquote><p>但是不能只靠這一句推出：</p><blockquote>Ben has a perfect life.</blockquote><p>因為後者加入了很多新意思。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Jane drinks water every day. 哪句抽象沒有放大證據？","options":[{"label":"Jane drinks something every day.","correct":true,"feedback":"對！water 是可以飲用的東西。"},{"label":"Jane never becomes ill.","correct":false,"feedback":"喝水不保證永遠不生病。"}]}},{"name":"一句話記住這個概念","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>正式名稱</h3><p><strong>概念抽象（Conceptual Abstraction）</strong></p>","<h3>學生名稱</h3><p><strong>具體 → 概念</strong></p>","<h3>核心問題</h3><blockquote><strong>文章給我的這個具體行為或能力，是不是答案中較大概念的一個清楚例子？</strong></blockquote><p>最簡單的模型是：</p><blockquote><strong>具體行為 → 它代表的較大概念</strong></blockquote><p>例如 run → exercise；cook by yourself → independence；give food and water → care。</p><p>這樣學生學到的就不只是一組字詞替換，更是<strong>如何把具體資訊提升到較大的意思層級</strong>。</p>"]}]},"3":{"title":"並列拆分","english":"Conjunction Elimination","short":"A 和 B，可以分開看","phases":["基礎拆分","共同資訊與三項清單","新資訊與 and / or","長句與精確拆分"],"stages":[{"name":"先掌握核心想法","accent":"gold","steps":["<strong>and 表示兩邊都成立。</strong>把其中一邊單獨拿出來，仍是原句已提供的資訊。","<blockquote>Mia bought a pen and a book.</blockquote><p>可以單獨知道她買了 a pen，也可以知道她買了 a book。</p>","<strong>共同條件要保留。</strong>不要把 or 當作 and，也不要自行加入新資訊。"]},{"name":"and 表示兩邊都成立","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>最基本的句子：</p><blockquote>Tom is tired and hungry.</blockquote><p>這句包含兩個資訊：</p><blockquote>Tom is tired.</blockquote><blockquote>Tom is hungry.</blockquote><p>所以，看到 and 時，可以先問：</p><blockquote>and 左邊是什麼？</blockquote><blockquote>and 右邊是什麼？</blockquote><p>如果兩邊都是同一句話中的真實資訊，就可以分開讀。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Tom is tired and hungry. 哪句一定包含在原句中？","options":[{"label":"Tom is tired.","correct":true,"feedback":"對！and 的兩邊都成立。"},{"label":"Tom is not hungry.","correct":false,"feedback":"原句同時說 Tom hungry。"}]}},{"name":"一個人做兩件事","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Example 1</h3><blockquote>Anna reads and writes every day.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Anna reads every day.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Anna writes every day.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>原句同時說明兩個動作：</p><p>• reads • writes</p><p>兩個動作都屬於 Anna。</p>","<h3>Example 2</h3><blockquote>Ben washed the car and cleaned the room.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Ben washed the car.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Ben cleaned the room.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>and 把兩個動作放在同一句中。</p><p>兩件事都發生了。</p>"]},{"name":"一個人有兩個東西","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Example 3</h3><blockquote>Lucy has a phone and a key.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Lucy has a phone.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Lucy has a key.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>phone 和 key 都屬於 Lucy。</p>","<h3>Example 4</h3><blockquote>David bought bread and water.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>David bought bread.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>David bought water.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>兩個東西都跟 bought 有關。</p>"]},{"name":"一個人有兩個特點","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>Example 5</h3><blockquote>Sam is young and strong.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Sam is young.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Sam is strong.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>young 和 strong 都在描述 Sam。</p>","<h3>Example 6</h3><blockquote>The bag is small and light.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>The bag is small.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>The bag is light.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>兩個形容詞都屬於同一個東西。</p>"]},{"name":"兩個人做同一件事","accent":"gold","steps":["<h3>Example 7</h3><blockquote>Amy and Paul are at school.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Amy is at school.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Paul is at school.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>and 連接兩個人。</p><p>後面的 are at school 同時適用於兩個人。</p>","<h3>Example 8</h3><blockquote>Jack and Leo play tennis after class.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Jack plays tennis after class.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Leo plays tennis after class.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>兩個人都做同一件事。</p>"]},{"name":"一個動作有兩個對象","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Example 9</h3><blockquote>Kate called Mary and John.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Kate called Mary.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Kate called John.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>Mary 和 John 都是 called 的對象。</p>","<h3>Example 10</h3><blockquote>The doctor spoke to Anna and Ben.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>The doctor spoke to Anna.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>The doctor spoke to Ben.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>同一個動作同時對兩個人發生。</p>"]},{"name":"較長的句子也可以分開","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Example 11</h3><blockquote>Peter sang and danced at the party.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Peter sang at the party.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Peter danced at the party.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>共同資訊要保留：</p><p>• Peter • at the party</p><p>改變的部分只有：</p><p>• sang • danced</p>","<h3>Example 12</h3><blockquote>Emma studied and ate in her room.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Emma studied in her room.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Emma ate in her room.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>in her room 同時跟兩個動作有關。</p><p>所以分開時，這個地點資訊要保留。</p>"]},{"name":"三個資訊也可以分開","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>Example 13</h3><blockquote>Mark can cook, swim, and drive.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Mark can cook.</blockquote><blockquote>Mark can swim.</blockquote><blockquote>Mark can drive.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>三個能力都已經在原句裡。</p><p>任何一個都可以單獨閱讀。</p>","<h3>Example 14</h3><blockquote>The box has a cup, a map, and a toy.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>The box has a cup.</blockquote><blockquote>The box has a map.</blockquote><blockquote>The box has a toy.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>清單中的每一項都屬於同一個 box。</p>"]},{"name":"both ... and ...","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>both ... and ... 會更清楚地表示：</p><blockquote>兩邊都成立。</blockquote>","<h3>Example 15</h3><blockquote>Lisa speaks both English and French.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Lisa speaks English.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Lisa speaks French.</blockquote>","<h3>Example 16</h3><blockquote>Both Tom and Mia are busy.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Tom is busy.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Mia is busy.</blockquote>"]},{"name":"完整句子也可以用 and 連接","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Example 17</h3><blockquote>Jane stayed home, and her brother went out.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Jane stayed home.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>Her brother went out.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>前後各自是一件完整事情。</p><p>and 表示兩件事都成立。</p>","<h3>Example 18</h3><blockquote>It was cold, and the street was quiet.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>It was cold.</blockquote><p>也可以知道：</p><blockquote>The street was quiet.</blockquote>"]},{"name":"分開時，要保留共同資訊","accent":"coral","steps":["<p>看：</p><blockquote>Mary reads and writes at night.</blockquote><p>完整分開：</p><blockquote>Mary reads at night.</blockquote><blockquote>Mary writes at night.</blockquote><p>如果只寫：</p><blockquote>Mary writes.</blockquote><p>內容仍然沒有錯，但少了 at night 這個資訊。</p><p>所以更好的做法是：</p><blockquote><strong>分開主要部分，同時保留仍然適用的共同資訊。</strong></blockquote>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Mary reads and writes at night. 哪句完整保留共同時間？","options":[{"label":"Mary writes at night.","correct":true,"feedback":"對！at night 仍然適用。"},{"label":"Mary writes every morning.","correct":false,"feedback":"原句沒有 every morning。"}]}},{"name":"不能自行加入新資訊","accent":"green","steps":["<p>這是最重要的限制之一。</p><p>已知：</p><blockquote>Tom is tired.</blockquote><p>不能直接寫：</p><blockquote>Tom is tired and hungry.</blockquote><p>因為 hungry 沒有來源。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 1</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>Emma can swim.</blockquote><p>錯誤：</p><blockquote>Emma can swim and drive.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼錯？</h3><p>drive 是新資訊。</p><p>原句沒有說 Emma can drive。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 2</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>The room is clean.</blockquote><p>錯誤：</p><blockquote>The room is clean and warm.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼錯？</h3><p>warm 沒有出現在原來的資訊中。</p>"]},{"name":"and 和 or 不能混在一起","accent":"gold","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 3</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>Ben will eat rice or noodles.</blockquote><p>錯誤：</p><blockquote>Ben will eat rice.</blockquote><p>也不能確定：</p><blockquote>Ben will eat noodles.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>or 表示其中一個可能成立。</p><p>它沒有告訴我們是哪一個。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 4</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>Lucy can take the bus or walk home.</blockquote><p>錯誤：</p><blockquote>Lucy will take the bus.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>原句保留兩個可能。</p><p>還缺少最後的選擇。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Ben will eat rice or noodles. 哪句一定成立？","options":[{"label":"他會吃其中一種，但目前不知道是哪種。","correct":true,"feedback":"對！or 保留選擇，尚未指定哪一邊。"},{"label":"Ben 一定吃 rice。","correct":false,"feedback":"or 不能當成 and 或指定 rice。"}]}},{"name":"小心共同資訊放錯位置","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 5</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>Ben cooked and ate in the kitchen.</blockquote><p>正確理解：</p><blockquote>Ben cooked in the kitchen.</blockquote><blockquote>Ben ate in the kitchen.</blockquote><p>錯誤理解：</p><blockquote>Ben cooked in the kitchen.</blockquote><blockquote>Ben ate somewhere else.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>原句中的 in the kitchen 放在兩個動作後面，正常理解會同時連到兩個動作。</p>"]},{"name":"小心主詞不能交換","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 6</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>Anna and Leo are tired.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Anna is tired.</blockquote><blockquote>Leo is tired.</blockquote><p>但不能寫：</p><blockquote>Anna is Leo.</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>and 只表示兩個人都具有 tired 這個狀態。</p><p>它沒有表示兩個人是同一個人。</p>"]},{"name":"判斷方法","accent":"green","steps":["<p>看到 and 或 both ... and ... 時，可以依序問三個問題：</p><p>• 1. <strong>and 連接了哪兩個部分？</strong> • 2. <strong>兩邊是否都真的成立？</strong> • 3. <strong>分開後，有沒有把共同資訊保留下來？</strong></p><p>最後再檢查：</p><blockquote>有沒有偷偷加入原句沒有提供的新資訊？</blockquote>"]},{"name":"核心規則","accent":"gold","steps":["<blockquote><strong>A 和 B 都成立時，A 可以單獨成立，B 也可以單獨成立。</strong></blockquote><p>例如：</p><blockquote>The car is old and slow.</blockquote><p>可以分成：</p><blockquote>The car is old.</blockquote><blockquote>The car is slow.</blockquote><p>但只有：</p><blockquote>The car is old.</blockquote><p>還不能加上：</p><blockquote>The car is slow.</blockquote><p>因為第二個資訊需要自己的證據。</p>"]}]},"4":{"title":"直接結果排除","english":"Direct Result Exclusion","short":"已完成的動作 → 排除直接衝突的結果","phases":["路線、位置與接觸","時間與選擇排除","完成、意圖與能力","直接性、原因與範圍"],"stages":[{"name":"先掌握核心想法","accent":"gold","steps":["<strong>動作已經完成</strong>，才能排除與它直接衝突的結果。","<blockquote>Nina goes around a hole.</blockquote><p>她走了旁邊的路，所以這一次沒有踏進洞裡。</p>","<strong>只排除直接結果。</strong>「想避開」、「可以避開」都不足以證明避開已發生；也不能因此猜測心情或原因。"]},{"name":"改變路線，可以排除原來路線上的結果","accent":"gold","steps":["<h3>Example 1</h3><blockquote>Nina goes around a hole.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Nina does not step into the hole.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>go around 表示她從旁邊經過。</p><p>所以她沒有進入 hole。</p><p>重點放在：</p><blockquote><strong>路線改變了，原來路線上的直接結果沒有發生。</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 2</h3><blockquote>Eric turns back before the bridge.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Eric does not cross the bridge.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>turns back before 表示他在到達 bridge 前回頭。</p><p>因此：</p><blockquote>cross the bridge</blockquote><p>沒有發生。</p><p>這裡被排除的是一個<strong>移動結果</strong>。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Nina goes around a hole. 哪個直接結果可排除？","options":[{"label":"Nina does not step into the hole.","correct":true,"feedback":"對！這一次的路線避開了洞。"},{"label":"Nina is afraid of holes.","correct":false,"feedback":"行動沒有交代她的感受。"}]}},{"name":"停在界線前，可以排除「越過」","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Example 3</h3><blockquote>Grace stops at the line.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Grace does not go past the line.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>stops at 表示她停在那個位置。</p><p>所以：</p><blockquote>go past the line</blockquote><p>和原句描述的結果不合。</p><p>被排除的是：</p><blockquote><strong>越過某個界線。</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 4</h3><blockquote>Leo stays on this side of the river.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Leo does not cross the river.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>this side of the river 說明 Leo 留在同一邊。</p><p>所以另一個結果：</p><blockquote>cross the river</blockquote><p>沒有發生。</p><p>這次的重點在<strong>位置</strong>，沒有使用碰撞的情境。</p>"]},{"name":"保持距離，可以排除直接接觸","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Example 5</h3><blockquote>Sophie keeps her hand away from the oven.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Sophie does not touch the oven.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>keeps her hand away 表示手和 oven 保持距離。</p><p>所以直接接觸沒有發生。</p><p>被排除的是：</p><blockquote><strong>touch</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 6</h3><blockquote>Adam keeps his feet out of the mud.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Adam does not step in the mud.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>keeps his feet out of 已經限制了 feet 的位置。</p><p>所以：</p><blockquote>step in the mud</blockquote><p>沒有發生。</p><p>這裡處理的是：</p><blockquote><strong>身體的一部分是否進入某個地方。</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"留在外面，可以排除「進入」","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>Example 7</h3><blockquote>Ruby waits outside the museum.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Ruby does not go into the museum.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>outside 和 go into 描述兩個不同位置。</p><p>Ruby 留在 outside，所以在這段時間內沒有進入 museum。</p><p>被排除的是：</p><blockquote><strong>entering a place</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 8</h3><blockquote>Daniel stays outside the gate.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Daniel does not go through the gate.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>他一直留在 gate 外面。</p><p>所以：</p><blockquote>go through the gate</blockquote><p>沒有發生。</p><p>這裡的關係來自<strong>位置限制</strong>。</p>"]},{"name":"提早離開，可以排除後面的參與","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>時間也可以形成直接結果排除。</p>","<h3>Example 9</h3><blockquote>Helen leaves the beach before the music starts.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Helen is not at the beach when the music starts.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>有兩個時間點：</p><p>• Helen leaves</p><p>• the music starts</p><p>before 告訴我們第一件事先發生。</p><p>所以第二件事開始時，Helen 已經離開。</p><p>被排除的是：</p><blockquote><strong>在那個時間仍然留在原地。</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 10</h3><blockquote>Oliver goes home before the meeting starts.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Oliver is not there when the meeting starts.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>goes home before 給出清楚的時間順序。</p><p>meeting 開始時，他已經離開原來的地方。</p><p>這裡沒有碰撞、物件或路線。</p><p>核心仍然相同：</p><blockquote>前面的行為排除了一個直接的後續情況。</blockquote>"]},{"name":"選一個方式，也可能排除另一個方式","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Example 11</h3><blockquote>Clara takes the stairs instead of the lift.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Clara does not use the lift.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>instead of 表示 Clara 選了其中一個方式。</p><p>她使用 stairs，所以這一次沒有使用 lift。</p><p>被排除的是：</p><blockquote><strong>另一個選擇。</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 12</h3><blockquote>Henry goes by boat instead of plane.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Henry does not travel by plane.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>原句已經說明他的交通方式是 boat。</p><p>instead of plane 同時排除了 plane。</p><p>這裡處理的是：</p><blockquote><strong>選擇排除另一個選擇。</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"直接結果排除可以有不同形式","accent":"coral","steps":["<p>前面的例子其實包含幾種不同的關係。</p>","<h3>1. 路線排除</h3><blockquote>go around a hole 所以沒有進入 hole</blockquote>","<h3>2. 界線排除</h3><blockquote>stop before a bridge</blockquote><blockquote>所以沒有過 bridge</blockquote>","<h3>3. 接觸排除</h3><blockquote>keep a hand away 所以沒有 touch</blockquote>","<h3>4. 位置排除</h3><blockquote>stay outside 所以沒有 enter</blockquote>","<h3>5. 時間排除</h3><blockquote>leave before something starts 所以開始時已經不在那裡</blockquote>","<h3>6. 選擇排除</h3><blockquote>choose one way instead of another 所以另一個方式沒有被使用</blockquote><p>共同點只有一個：</p><blockquote><strong>原句中的資訊，讓另一個直接衝突的結果無法同時成立。</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"被排除的結果要夠「直接」","accent":"green","steps":["<p>已知：</p><blockquote>Ava stays outside the library.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Ava does not enter the library.</blockquote><p>兩個資訊都在談：</p><p>• Ava • library • inside / outside</p><p>關係非常近。</p><p>但不能因此說：</p><blockquote>Ava does not like books.</blockquote><p>does not like books 加入了新的感受。</p><p>原句沒有提供這個資訊。</p>","<h3>Example 13</h3><blockquote>Kevin stops before the river.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Kevin does not cross the river.</blockquote><p>不能因此知道：</p><blockquote>Kevin is afraid of water.</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>does not cross 和他的動作直接有關。</p><p>afraid 談的是內心感受，需要其他資訊。</p>"]},{"name":"「想做」和「真的做到」要分開","accent":"gold","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 1</h3><blockquote>Alice tries to stay outside the field.</blockquote><p>不能確定：</p><blockquote>Alice does not enter the field.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>tries to 只說她有這個目標。</p><p>最後成功了沒有，原句沒有交代。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 2</h3><blockquote>Mark wants to stop before the river.</blockquote><p>不能確定：</p><blockquote>Mark does not cross the river.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>wants to 描述想法。</p><p>它沒有告訴我們最後的行動。</p><p>所以：</p><blockquote><strong>目標</strong></blockquote><p>和</p><blockquote><strong>完成的結果</strong></blockquote><p>需要分開。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Alice tries to stay outside the field. 能確定她沒有進去嗎？","options":[{"label":"不能，tries to 只表示嘗試。","correct":true,"feedback":"對！原句沒有交代結果。"},{"label":"能，嘗試等於已完成。","correct":false,"feedback":"目標與已完成的結果不同。"}]}},{"name":"「有能力」也不能當成「已經完成」","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 3</h3><blockquote>Emma can stay outside the building.</blockquote><p>不能確定：</p><blockquote>Emma stays outside the building.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>can 表示有能力或有選擇。</p><p>她最後也可能進去。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 4</h3><blockquote>Jack can take another path.</blockquote><p>不能確定：</p><blockquote>Jack does not use this path.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>他有另一個選擇，不等於他真的用了另一個選擇。</p>"]},{"name":"結果不能放大得太遠","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 5</h3><blockquote>Laura goes around the mud.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Laura does not step into the mud.</blockquote><p>但不能因此知道：</p><blockquote>Laura&#x27;s shoes are clean all day.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>原句只處理眼前的一個地方。</p><p>她之後還可能走到其他地方。</p><p>all day 把範圍放大了很多。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 6</h3><blockquote>Peter stays outside the stadium.</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Peter does not enter the stadium.</blockquote><p>但不能因此知道：</p><blockquote>Peter is safe.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>safe 涉及很多可能情況。</p><p>原句只提供一個位置資訊。</p>"]},{"name":"不能自己加入原因","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 7</h3><blockquote>Sarah leaves before dinner.</blockquote><p>不能因此知道：</p><blockquote>Sarah does not like the food.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>她提早離開可能有很多原因：</p><p>• she is tired • she has work • she needs to go home</p><p>原句沒有說明原因。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 8</h3><blockquote>David waits outside the cinema.</blockquote><p>不能因此知道：</p><blockquote>David does not like films.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>waits outside 描述位置。</p><p>does not like films 描述喜好。</p><p>兩者之間缺少資訊。</p>"]},{"name":"反過來也要小心","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>有時只知道某個結果沒有發生，仍然不知道他用了什麼方法。</p><p>例如：</p><blockquote>Maria does not cross the bridge.</blockquote><p>不能因此知道：</p><blockquote>Maria turns back before the bridge.</blockquote><p>她也可能：</p><p>• never go near the bridge • stop for a long time • take another way</p><p>同一個結果，可以有不同原因或方法。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 9</h3><blockquote>James does not enter the garden.</blockquote><p>不能確定：</p><blockquote>James waits outside the garden.</blockquote>","<h3>原因</h3><p>他可能根本沒有去 garden。</p><p>所以：</p><blockquote><strong>沒有發生某結果</strong></blockquote><p>通常不能直接告訴我們：</p><blockquote><strong>用了哪一個方法避免它。</strong></blockquote>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Maria does not cross the bridge. 能確定她回頭嗎？","options":[{"label":"不能；她也可能根本沒有靠近橋。","correct":true,"feedback":"對！同一個結果可能有不同原因。"},{"label":"能；不過橋只可能是回頭。","correct":false,"feedback":"沒有過橋不會指定避免的方法。"}]}},{"name":"判斷時看四件事","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>第一：動作真的完成了嗎？</h3><p>較強：</p><blockquote>stays stops leaves goes around keeps away</blockquote><p>較弱：</p><blockquote>tries wants can may</blockquote>","<h3>第二：被排除的結果和原句是否很接近？</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>stay outside a place</blockquote><p>和：</p><blockquote>enter that place</blockquote><p>關係很直接。</p>","<h3>第三：人、地點、時間是否相同？</h3><p>如果原句說：</p><blockquote>outside the museum</blockquote><p>答案卻談：</p><blockquote>another building</blockquote><p>資訊就換掉了。</p>","<h3>第四：答案有沒有加入新的原因、感受或很大的結果？</h3><p>特別留意：</p><blockquote>afraid like happy safe all day always never</blockquote><p>這些詞常常讓答案超過原句能支持的範圍。</p>"]},{"name":"核心規則","accent":"coral","steps":["<p>名稱：</p><blockquote><strong>直接結果排除 Direct Result Exclusion</strong></blockquote><p>核心問題：</p><blockquote><strong>原句中的行為已經完成後，哪一個和它直接衝突的結果就不能同時成立？</strong></blockquote><p>例如：</p><blockquote>stay outside a place</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>do not enter that place.</blockquote><blockquote>leave before an event starts</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>not be there when it starts.</blockquote>","<blockquote>use one way instead of another</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>do not use the other way.</blockquote><p>判斷時抓住三點：</p><p><strong>動作已完成、結果很直接、範圍保持相同。</strong></p>"]}]},"5":{"title":"預防性因果推理","english":"Preventive Causal Reasoning","short":"事前行動 → 降低問題風險","phases":["行動真正預防甚麼","預防與減少後果","假因果、意圖與過強結果","多步預防與因果陷阱"],"stages":[{"name":"先掌握核心想法","accent":"gold","steps":["<strong>預防性因果</strong>關心的是：事前行動怎樣減少之後的問題。","<blockquote>Save work often → lower the risk of losing it.</blockquote><p>要找出行動和問題之間清楚的機制。</p>","<strong>有助於，不等於保證。</strong>預防措施通常降低風險，不能寫成 always、never 或 completely safe。"]},{"name":"最直接的預防：先保護自己","accent":"gold","steps":["<h3>Example 1</h3><blockquote>Mia washes her hands before lunch.</blockquote><blockquote>（Mia 午餐前會洗手。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps her stay healthy.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於她保持健康。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>手上可能有不乾淨的東西。</p><p>先洗手，可以減少把它們帶進嘴裡的機會。</p><p>重點：</p><blockquote><strong>先清潔，減少健康問題。</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 2</h3><blockquote>Kevin wears gloves when he holds a hot pan.</blockquote><blockquote>（Kevin 拿很熱的平底鍋時會戴手套。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps protect his hands.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於保護他的手。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>hot pan 可能傷到手。</p><p>gloves 放在手和熱的東西中間，可以減少受傷的機會。</p>","<h3>Example 3</h3><blockquote>Eva wears a helmet when she rides her bike.</blockquote><blockquote>（Eva 騎腳踏車時會戴安全帽。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps protect her head.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於保護她的頭部。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>helmet 的作用和 head 直接有關。</p><p>如果發生問題，頭部可以得到更多保護。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Mia 午餐前洗手，最直接能減少哪個問題？","options":[{"label":"手上的髒東西進入口中。","correct":true,"feedback":"對！洗手與進食衛生有直接關係。"},{"label":"午餐一定不會變涼。","correct":false,"feedback":"洗手不能保證食物溫度。"}]}},{"name":"先檢查，再行動","accent":"blue","steps":["<p>有些預防不是使用保護物，而是：</p><blockquote><strong>先看看有沒有問題。</strong></blockquote>","<h3>Example 4</h3><blockquote>Daniel checks the chair before he sits down.</blockquote><blockquote>（Daniel 坐下前會先檢查椅子。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps him sit down more safely.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於他更安全地坐下。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>如果 chair 有問題，先檢查就有機會發現。</p><p>先發現問題，可以減少後面的危險。</p>","<h3>Example 5</h3><blockquote>Sophie checks the door before she leaves home.</blockquote><blockquote>（Sophie 離開家前會檢查門。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps keep her home safe.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於讓她的家更安全。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>檢查 door 可以確認它有沒有關好。</p><p>問題先被發現，後面出現麻煩的機會就會降低。</p>","<h3>Example 6</h3><blockquote>Adam reads the name before he sends the message.</blockquote><blockquote>（Adam 傳送訊息前會先看名字。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps him send the message to the right person.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於他把訊息傳給正確的人。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>如果沒有先看名字，message 可能傳錯人。</p><p>先檢查名字，可以減少這種錯誤。</p><p>這裡預防的不是身體上的危險，而是：</p><blockquote><strong>mistake</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"提前準備，可以減少後面的問題","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Example 7</h3><blockquote>Grace puts her school books in her bag at night.</blockquote><blockquote>（Grace 晚上先把課本放進書包。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps her remember her books in the morning.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於她早上記得帶課本。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>晚上先準備好，早上需要做的事情就比較少。</p><p>所以忘記 books 的機會會降低。</p>","<h3>Example 8</h3><blockquote>Leo sets an alarm before he goes to bed.</blockquote><blockquote>（Leo 睡覺前會設定鬧鐘。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps him get up on time.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於他準時起床。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>alarm 在需要起床的時間提醒他。</p><p>所以睡過頭的機會比較低。</p>","<h3>Example 9</h3><blockquote>Nina charges her phone before school.</blockquote><blockquote>（Nina 上學前會先幫手機充電。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps keep her phone on during the day.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於讓她的手機白天保持有電。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>如果 phone 沒有足夠的電，它可能很快關掉。</p><p>先充電，可以減少這個問題。</p>"]},{"name":"控制環境，也可以預防問題","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>Example 10</h3><blockquote>Oliver closes the window before the rain starts.</blockquote><blockquote>（Oliver 在下雨前先把窗戶關起來。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps keep the room dry.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於讓房間保持乾燥。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>window 開著時，rain 可能進到房間。</p><p>先關窗，可以減少水進來的機會。</p>","<h3>Example 11</h3><blockquote>Ruby puts the milk in the fridge.</blockquote><blockquote>（Ruby 把牛奶放進冰箱。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps keep the milk fresh.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於讓牛奶保持新鮮。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>fridge 的低溫可以幫助食物保存。</p><p>這裡的預防目標是：</p><blockquote>food going bad</blockquote>","<h3>Example 12</h3><blockquote>Henry puts the lid on his water bottle.</blockquote><blockquote>（Henry 把水瓶的蓋子蓋好。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps stop water from coming out.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於防止水流出來。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>lid 關好後，water 比較不容易流到外面。</p><p>預防的問題是：</p><blockquote>water coming out</blockquote>"]},{"name":"關掉某個東西，也可能是在預防問題","accent":"gold","steps":["<h3>Example 13</h3><blockquote>Clara turns off the stove after cooking.</blockquote><blockquote>（Clara 做完飯後會關掉爐子。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps make the kitchen safer.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於讓廚房更安全。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>stove 如果一直開著，可能帶來危險。</p><p>做完飯後關掉，可以減少問題發生的機會。</p>","<h3>Example 14</h3><blockquote>Max turns off the water before he leaves the bathroom.</blockquote><blockquote>（Max 離開浴室前會把水關掉。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps stop water from filling the room.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於防止水一直流進房間。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>水一直開著，可能流出來。</p><p>先關掉，可以避免後面的麻煩。</p>"]},{"name":"保存資料，也有預防性因果關係","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Example 15</h3><blockquote>Emma saves her work often on the computer.</blockquote><blockquote>（Emma 在電腦上常常儲存自己的工作。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps her keep her work if the computer stops.</blockquote><blockquote>（如果電腦停止運作，這有助於她保留自己的工作。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>computer 可能突然停止。</p><p>如果已經先 save，失去全部工作的機會會降低。</p><p>這裡的預防目標是：</p><blockquote>losing work</blockquote>","<h3>Example 16</h3><blockquote>Paul makes a copy of an important photo.</blockquote><blockquote>（Paul 會為重要的照片多存一份。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps him keep the photo if one copy is lost.</blockquote><blockquote>（如果其中一份不見了，這有助於他保留那張照片。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>多一份 copy，代表出現問題時還有另一份。</p><p>預防的問題是：</p><blockquote>losing the only copy</blockquote>"]},{"name":"預防性因果推理不限於「安全」","accent":"coral","steps":["<p>前面的例子可以分成很多類：</p>","<h3>身體保護</h3><blockquote>wear gloves （戴手套） wear a helmet （戴安全帽）</blockquote>","<h3>錯誤預防</h3><blockquote>check a name before sending （傳送前檢查名字）</blockquote>","<h3>忘記事情</h3><blockquote>prepare books at night （晚上先準備課本）</blockquote>","<h3>時間問題</h3><blockquote>set an alarm （設定鬧鐘）</blockquote>","<h3>物品保存</h3><blockquote>put milk in the fridge （把牛奶放進冰箱）</blockquote>","<h3>資料保護</h3><blockquote>save computer work （儲存電腦上的工作）</blockquote><p>所以核心範圍比「避免危險」更大。</p><p>它也可以處理：</p><blockquote><strong>避免錯誤、避免損失、避免忘記、避免損壞。</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"一個很重要的界線：降低機會，不代表保證結果","accent":"green","steps":["<p>看：</p><blockquote>Leo sets an alarm before bed.</blockquote><blockquote>（Leo 睡前會設定鬧鐘。）</blockquote><p>可以支持：</p><blockquote>This helps him get up on time.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於他準時起床。）</blockquote><p>但不能確定：</p><blockquote>Leo will always get up on time.</blockquote><blockquote>（Leo 永遠都會準時起床。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>alarm 可以幫助他。</p><p>他仍然可能：</p><p>• 沒有聽到 • 關掉 alarm • 又睡著</p><p>所以預防性因果推理通常表示：</p><blockquote><strong>問題比較不容易發生。</strong></blockquote><p>它很少表示：</p><blockquote><strong>問題完全不可能發生。</strong></blockquote>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Leo 設鬧鐘。哪個說法不把結果說得過強？","options":[{"label":"這有助於他準時起床。","correct":true,"feedback":"對！鬧鐘可以降低遲起風險。"},{"label":"他今後永遠不會睡過頭。","correct":false,"feedback":"鬧鐘不保證永遠有效。"}]}},{"name":"Wrong Cases：行動和問題之間要有真實關係","accent":"gold","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 1</h3><blockquote>Anna wears a green shirt before a test.</blockquote><blockquote>（Anna 考試前會穿綠色上衣。）</blockquote><p>不能因此知道：</p><blockquote>This helps her get a better score.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於她得到更好的分數。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>green shirt 和 test score 之間沒有清楚的預防關係。</p><p>需要更多資訊才能把兩件事連起來。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 2</h3><blockquote>Jack takes a spoon to school.</blockquote><blockquote>（Jack 帶一支湯匙去學校。）</blockquote><p>不能因此知道：</p><blockquote>This helps him remember his homework.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於他記得帶功課。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>spoon 和 homework 之間沒有直接關係。</p><p>一個行動存在，不代表它一定能預防某個問題。</p>"]},{"name":"Wrong Cases：想做，和真的做，要分清楚","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 3</h3><blockquote>Mia plans to save her work.</blockquote><blockquote>（Mia 打算儲存自己的工作。）</blockquote><p>不能確定：</p><blockquote>Her work is safe.</blockquote><blockquote>（她的工作已經安全保存。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>plans to 只表示計畫。</p><p>真正的 save 是否完成，還不知道。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 4</h3><blockquote>Ben wants to close the window.</blockquote><blockquote>（Ben 想把窗戶關起來。）</blockquote><p>不能確定：</p><blockquote>The room stays dry.</blockquote><blockquote>（房間會保持乾燥。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>wants to 描述想法。</p><p>window 最後有沒有關上，原句沒有說。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Mia plans to save her work. 可以確定資料已保存嗎？","options":[{"label":"不能；計畫尚未等於完成。","correct":true,"feedback":"對！須確認行動實際發生。"},{"label":"可以；想做就代表做好。","correct":false,"feedback":"plans to 只描述意圖。"}]}},{"name":"Wrong Cases：不能把結果說得太強","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 5</h3><blockquote>Eva puts her phone in a case.</blockquote><blockquote>（Eva 把手機放進保護殼。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps protect the phone.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於保護手機。）</blockquote><p>但不能確定：</p><blockquote>Her phone can never break.</blockquote><blockquote>（她的手機永遠不會壞。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>case 可以減少一些損壞。</p><p>never break 的範圍太強。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 6</h3><blockquote>Daniel checks the door before bed.</blockquote><blockquote>（Daniel 睡前會檢查門。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>This helps keep the home safer.</blockquote><blockquote>（這有助於讓家裡更安全。）</blockquote><p>但不能確定：</p><blockquote>Nothing bad can happen.</blockquote><blockquote>（任何壞事都不可能發生。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼？</h3><p>檢查 door 只減少一部分問題。</p><p>其他問題仍然可能發生。</p>"]},{"name":"判斷時可以問四個問題","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>1. 後面有沒有一個清楚的問題？</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>lose work （失去工作內容） forget books （忘記帶書） send a message to the wrong person （把訊息傳錯人）</blockquote>","<h3>2. 前面的行動真的能減少這個問題嗎？</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>save work often （常常儲存工作）</blockquote><p>和：</p><blockquote>lose work （失去工作內容）</blockquote><p>關係很清楚。</p>","<h3>3. 行動真的發生了嗎？</h3><p>比較：</p><blockquote>Nina charges her phone.</blockquote><blockquote>（Nina 幫手機充電。）</blockquote><p>和：</p><blockquote>Nina wants to charge her phone.</blockquote><blockquote>（Nina 想幫手機充電。）</blockquote><p>第二句只說想法。</p>","<h3>4. 結果有沒有說得太強？</h3><p>較合理：</p><blockquote>helps protect （有助於保護） helps stop （有助於防止） helps keep （有助於保持） makes something safer （讓某件事更安全）</blockquote><p>需要小心：</p><blockquote>always （總是）</blockquote><blockquote>never （永遠不） completely safe （完全安全）</blockquote>"]},{"name":"核心規則","accent":"gold","steps":["<h3>預防性因果推理</h3>","<h3>Preventive Causal Reasoning</h3><p>一個簡單的判斷方式：</p><blockquote><strong>先問：可能出什麼問題？</strong></blockquote><p>再問：</p><blockquote><strong>這個行動有沒有在問題發生前，減少它發生的機會？</strong></blockquote><p>如果兩者有清楚的因果關係，就可以理解成預防性因果推理。</p><p>例如：</p><blockquote>save work often （常常儲存工作）</blockquote><p>可以減少：</p><blockquote>lose all the work （失去全部工作內容）</blockquote><p>或者：</p><blockquote>check the name before sending （傳送前檢查名字）</blockquote><p>可以減少：</p>","<blockquote>send it to the wrong person （傳給錯的人）</blockquote><p>最重要的界線：</p><blockquote><strong>預防代表降低問題發生的機會，通常不代表百分之百保證問題永遠不會發生。</strong></blockquote>"]}]},"6":{"title":"關係方向與角色次序","english":"Non-symmetric Relations","short":"誰做事、對誰做","phases":["基礎角色方向","時間、比較與反方向","角色交換與對稱例外","多關係與角色陷阱"],"stages":[{"name":"先掌握核心想法","accent":"gold","steps":["<strong>先確認兩個角色：</strong>誰做事？動作對誰發生？","<blockquote>Alice sends a card to David.</blockquote><p>Alice 是寄件人；David 是收件人。直接交換名字會改變事件。</p>","<strong>換視角時可能要換詞。</strong>give / receive、before / after 可以描述同一關係；like / call 的反方向則未必有證據。"]},{"name":"先找「誰做事」","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>最簡單的方法，是先找動作前面的人。</p>","<h3>Example 1</h3><blockquote>Emily visits her aunt.</blockquote><blockquote>（Emily 去探望她的阿姨。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Emily is the visitor.</blockquote><blockquote>（Emily 是去探望別人的人。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>Her aunt visits Emily.</blockquote><blockquote>（她的阿姨去探望 Emily。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>原句只說 Emily 去找 aunt。</p><p>aunt 有沒有去找 Emily，沒有交代。</p>","<h3>Example 2</h3><blockquote>Jason follows his brother.</blockquote><blockquote>（Jason 跟著他的哥哥。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Jason is behind his brother.</blockquote><blockquote>（Jason 跟在哥哥後面。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>His brother follows Jason.</blockquote><blockquote>（他的哥哥跟著 Jason。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>follow 有清楚的方向。</p><p>一個人在前面，另一個人在後面。</p><p>角色交換後，情況就變了。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Emily visits her aunt. 哪句保留角色方向？","options":[{"label":"Emily 是探訪者。","correct":true,"feedback":"對！Emily 做 visits 這個動作。"},{"label":"她的阿姨是探訪者。","correct":false,"feedback":"把探訪者和被探訪者交換了。"}]}},{"name":"再找「動作對誰發生」","accent":"blue","steps":["<p>有些句子的重點在受詞。</p>","<h3>Example 3</h3><blockquote>Chloe invites Eric to dinner.</blockquote><blockquote>（Chloe 邀請 Eric 吃晚餐。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Eric gets the invitation.</blockquote><blockquote>（Eric 收到邀請。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>Eric invites Chloe to dinner.</blockquote><blockquote>（Eric 邀請 Chloe 吃晚餐。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>invite 有兩個角色：</p><p>• 發出邀請的人 • 收到邀請的人</p><p>兩個角色不能自行交換。</p>","<h3>Example 4</h3><blockquote>Ryan teaches Lily English.</blockquote><blockquote>（Ryan 教 Lily 英文。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Ryan is the teacher in this situation.</blockquote><blockquote>（在這個情況中，Ryan 是教的人。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>Lily teaches Ryan English.</blockquote><blockquote>（Lily 教 Ryan 英文。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>teach 的方向很清楚。</p><p>誰教誰，需要按照原句的位置理解。</p>"]},{"name":"給東西和收到東西，方向不同","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Example 5</h3><blockquote>Maria gives Sam a key.</blockquote><blockquote>（Maria 給 Sam 一把鑰匙。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Sam gets a key from Maria.</blockquote><blockquote>（Sam 從 Maria 那裡拿到一把鑰匙。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>Sam gives Maria a key.</blockquote><blockquote>（Sam 給 Maria 一把鑰匙。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>同一件事可以從兩個角度描述：</p><blockquote>Maria gives.</blockquote><p>以及：</p><blockquote>Sam gets.</blockquote><p>但如果把 giver 和 receiver 交換，資訊就改變了。</p>","<h3>Example 6</h3><blockquote>Henry sends a photo to his mother.</blockquote><blockquote>（Henry 傳一張照片給他的媽媽。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>His mother gets the photo from Henry.</blockquote><blockquote>（他的媽媽從 Henry 那裡收到照片。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>His mother sends a photo to Henry.</blockquote><blockquote>（他的媽媽傳一張照片給 Henry。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>send 有起點，也有終點。</p><p>起點和終點交換後，會變成另一件事。</p>"]},{"name":"借和還也有角色方向","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>Example 7</h3><blockquote>Olivia borrows a book from Kate.</blockquote><blockquote>（Olivia 向 Kate 借一本書。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Olivia gets the book from Kate for some time.</blockquote><blockquote>（Olivia 暫時從 Kate 那裡拿到那本書。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>Kate borrows a book from Olivia.</blockquote><blockquote>（Kate 向 Olivia 借一本書。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>borrow from 裡面有方向：</p><blockquote>東西從 Kate 那裡到 Olivia 那裡。</blockquote><p>交換兩個人後，方向也跟著改了。</p>","<h3>Example 8</h3><blockquote>George returns the bag to Helen.</blockquote><blockquote>（George 把袋子還給 Helen。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Helen gets the bag back.</blockquote><blockquote>（Helen 拿回那個袋子。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>Helen returns the bag to George.</blockquote><blockquote>（Helen 把袋子還給 George。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>return ... to ... 也有清楚的角色：</p><p>• 誰還東西 • 東西還給誰</p>"]},{"name":"位置關係也有方向","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>有些句子沒有明顯的動作，但位置仍然有方向。</p>","<h3>Example 9</h3><blockquote>The lamp is above the table.</blockquote><blockquote>（燈在桌子的上方。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>The table is below the lamp.</blockquote><blockquote>（桌子在燈的下方。）</blockquote><p>不能說：</p><blockquote>The table is above the lamp.</blockquote><blockquote>（桌子在燈的上方。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>above 和 below 是一組有方向的位置關係。</p><p>交換兩個物件時，關係詞也需要跟著改。</p>","<h3>Example 10</h3><blockquote>The shop is behind the bank.</blockquote><blockquote>（商店在銀行後面。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>The bank is in front of the shop.</blockquote><blockquote>（銀行在商店前面。）</blockquote><p>不能直接說：</p><blockquote>The bank is behind the shop.</blockquote><blockquote>（銀行在商店後面。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>角色交換後，位置詞也要改變。</p>"]},{"name":"時間順序不能交換","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>Example 11</h3><blockquote>Breakfast comes before lunch.</blockquote><blockquote>（早餐在午餐之前。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Lunch comes after breakfast.</blockquote><blockquote>（午餐在早餐之後。）</blockquote><p>不能說：</p><blockquote>Lunch comes before breakfast.</blockquote><blockquote>（午餐在早餐之前。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>before 和 after 有固定方向。</p><p>交換兩個事件後，需要使用另一個關係詞。</p>","<h3>Example 12</h3><blockquote>The lesson starts before the game.</blockquote><blockquote>（課堂在比賽之前開始。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>The game starts after the lesson.</blockquote><blockquote>（比賽在課堂之後開始。）</blockquote><p>不能說：</p><blockquote>The game starts before the lesson.</blockquote><blockquote>（比賽在課堂之前開始。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>時間順序一旦確定，前後位置就不能自由交換。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Breakfast comes before lunch. 換視角如何正確表達？","options":[{"label":"Lunch comes after breakfast.","correct":true,"feedback":"對！角色交換，before 要換成 after。"},{"label":"Lunch comes before breakfast.","correct":false,"feedback":"交換後仍用 before 會倒轉時間。"}]}},{"name":"比較關係有更強的方向限制","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Example 13</h3><blockquote>Anna is older than Lucy.</blockquote><blockquote>（Anna 比 Lucy 年長。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Lucy is younger than Anna.</blockquote><blockquote>（Lucy 比 Anna 年輕。）</blockquote><p>不能說：</p><blockquote>Lucy is older than Anna.</blockquote><blockquote>（Lucy 比 Anna 年長。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>older than 有固定方向。</p><p>如果 Anna 比 Lucy 年長，反過來就要改成：</p><blockquote>younger than</blockquote>","<h3>Example 14</h3><blockquote>This box is heavier than that box.</blockquote><blockquote>（這個箱子比那個箱子重。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>That box is lighter than this box.</blockquote><blockquote>（那個箱子比這個箱子輕。）</blockquote><p>不能說：</p><blockquote>That box is heavier than this box.</blockquote><blockquote>（那個箱子比這個箱子重。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>比較句中：</p><p>• 哪一個比較重 • 哪一個比較輕</p><p>角色位置非常重要。</p>"]},{"name":"有些關係交換後一定錯","accent":"green","steps":["<p>像下面這些關係，方向非常強：</p><blockquote>older than （比……年長） before （在……之前） above （在……上方）</blockquote><p>如果原來的方向成立，把兩邊直接交換，原句的關係就會出問題。</p><p>例如：</p><blockquote>May is older than Kim.</blockquote><blockquote>（May 比 Kim 年長。）</blockquote><p>直接交換成：</p><blockquote>Kim is older than May.</blockquote><blockquote>（Kim 比 May 年長。）</blockquote><p>兩句不能同時描述同一個年齡關係。</p>"]},{"name":"有些關係交換後「可能也成立」，但目前不知道","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>另一類更需要小心。</p><p>例如：</p><blockquote>Peter likes Susan.</blockquote><blockquote>（Peter 喜歡 Susan。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>Susan likes Peter.</blockquote><blockquote>（Susan 喜歡 Peter。）</blockquote><p>Susan 也許喜歡 Peter，也許不喜歡。</p><p>原句沒有提供答案。</p>","<h3>Example 15</h3><blockquote>Rachel helps her neighbour.</blockquote><blockquote>（Rachel 幫助她的鄰居。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>Her neighbour helps Rachel.</blockquote><blockquote>（她的鄰居幫助 Rachel。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>兩件事可以同時發生。</p><p>但只知道第一件事時，第二件事仍然沒有證據。</p>","<h3>Example 16</h3><blockquote>Andrew calls his cousin every Sunday.</blockquote><blockquote>（Andrew 每個星期日都打電話給他的表兄弟。）</blockquote><p>不能直接知道：</p><blockquote>His cousin calls Andrew every Sunday.</blockquote><blockquote>（他的表兄弟每個星期日都打電話給 Andrew。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>對方可能也會打電話。</p><p>但原句只說 Andrew 主動打電話。</p>"]},{"name":"兩種「方向不能交換」要分清楚","accent":"blue","steps":["<h3>第一類：交換後會和原來的關係衝突</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>older than before above</blockquote><p>如果 A 在 B 之前，B 就不能同時在 A 之前。</p>","<h3>第二類：交換後可能成立，也可能不成立</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>like call visit help</blockquote><p>如果 A 幫 B，我們只能確定：</p><blockquote>A 幫 B。</blockquote><p>至於：</p><blockquote>B 有沒有幫 A</blockquote><p>還需要新的資訊。</p><p>這個區別很重要。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"Peter likes Susan. 能否確定 Susan likes Peter？","options":[{"label":"不能；反方向未提供資料。","correct":true,"feedback":"對！Susan 可能喜歡，也可能不喜歡。"},{"label":"能；likes 一定是雙向。","correct":false,"feedback":"likes 並非必然雙向。"}]}},{"name":"Wrong Cases：不能只看相同的人和動詞","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 1</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>Laura invites Kevin to a party.</blockquote><blockquote>（Laura 邀請 Kevin 參加派對。）</blockquote><p>錯誤理解：</p><blockquote>Kevin invites Laura to a party.</blockquote><blockquote>（Kevin 邀請 Laura 參加派對。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼有問題？</h3><p>人名都一樣，動詞也一樣。</p><p>但兩個人的角色交換了。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 2</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>The cat is under the chair.</blockquote><blockquote>（貓在椅子下面。）</blockquote><p>錯誤理解：</p><blockquote>The chair is under the cat.</blockquote><blockquote>（椅子在貓下面。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼有問題？</h3><p>交換兩個物件後，under 不能保持原樣。</p><p>正確的另一個角度會使用：</p><blockquote>above</blockquote>"]},{"name":"Wrong Cases：改成相反詞時，也要一起交換角色","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>Wrong Case 3</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>June is taller than Amy.</blockquote><blockquote>（June 比 Amy 高。）</blockquote><p>正確的另一個說法：</p><blockquote>Amy is shorter than June.</blockquote><blockquote>（Amy 比 June 矮。）</blockquote><p>錯誤：</p><blockquote>Amy is shorter than June, so June is shorter than Amy.</blockquote><blockquote>（Amy 比 June 矮，所以 June 比 Amy 矮。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼有問題？</h3><p>taller 和 shorter 的方向受到兩個人的位置控制。</p><p>不能在後面再次交換。</p>","<h3>Wrong Case 4</h3><p>已知：</p><blockquote>The film starts after dinner.</blockquote><blockquote>（電影在晚餐之後開始。）</blockquote><p>正確理解：</p><blockquote>Dinner comes before the film.</blockquote><blockquote>（晚餐在電影之前。）</blockquote><p>錯誤：</p><blockquote>Dinner comes after the film.</blockquote><blockquote>（晚餐在電影之後。）</blockquote>","<h3>為什麼有問題？</h3><p>交換兩邊後，時間詞也必須跟著改。</p>"]},{"name":"看到關係句，可以先找三個部分","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>例如：</p><blockquote>Lucy sends a letter to Mark.</blockquote><blockquote>（Lucy 寄一封信給 Mark。）</blockquote><p>先找：</p>","<h3>誰開始這個動作？</h3><blockquote>Lucy</blockquote>","<h3>做什麼？</h3><blockquote>sends a letter</blockquote>","<h3>動作去向誰？</h3><blockquote>Mark</blockquote><p>把三個位置看清楚後，會得到：</p><blockquote>Lucy → sender Mark → receiver</blockquote><p>實際閱讀時不需要使用任何符號，只要記住：</p><blockquote><strong>誰做、做什麼、對誰做。</strong></blockquote>"]},{"name":"位置句可以問另外三個問題","accent":"blue","steps":["<p>例如：</p><blockquote>The bus stop is next to the library.</blockquote><blockquote>（巴士站在圖書館旁邊。）</blockquote><p>有些位置關係可以交換：</p><blockquote>The library is next to the bus stop.</blockquote><blockquote>（圖書館在巴士站旁邊。）</blockquote><p>因為 next to 通常沒有方向差別。</p><p>所以「角色方向不能交換」不能套用到所有關係詞。</p>"]},{"name":"有些關係本身可以交換","accent":"coral","steps":["<h3>Example 17</h3><blockquote>Emma and Zoe are sisters.</blockquote><blockquote>（Emma 和 Zoe 是姊妹。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>Zoe and Emma are sisters.</blockquote><blockquote>（Zoe 和 Emma 是姊妹。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>sisters 描述雙方共有的關係。</p><p>交換名字後，關係仍然成立。</p>","<h3>Example 18</h3><blockquote>The café is next to the school.</blockquote><blockquote>（咖啡店在學校旁邊。）</blockquote><p>可以知道：</p><blockquote>The school is next to the café.</blockquote><blockquote>（學校在咖啡店旁邊。）</blockquote>","<h3>解釋</h3><p>next to 沒有前後方向。</p><p>所以交換位置仍然保留原來的關係。</p>"],"quiz":{"prompt":"The café is next to the school. 哪句仍然成立？","options":[{"label":"The school is next to the café.","correct":true,"feedback":"對！next to 通常可交換兩個位置。"},{"label":"The school is above the café.","correct":false,"feedback":"原句沒有上下關係。"}]}},{"name":"判斷時問三個問題","accent":"green","steps":["<h3>第一個問題：兩個角色一樣嗎？</h3><p>看清楚：</p><blockquote>誰做事？</blockquote><blockquote>誰接受動作？</blockquote>","<h3>第二個問題：關係有方向嗎？</h3><p>常見的方向關係：</p><blockquote>send give follow visit teach before above older than</blockquote>","<h3>第三個問題：交換後，需要換另一個詞嗎？</h3><p>例如：</p><blockquote>give → get （給 → 收到） above → below （上方 → 下方） before → after （之前 → 之後） older → younger （年長 → 年輕）</blockquote><p>如果角色交換後關係詞也需要改，原來的詞就不能直接保留。</p>"]},{"name":"核心規則","accent":"gold","steps":["<p>正式名稱：</p><blockquote><strong>非對稱關係 Non-symmetric Relations</strong></blockquote><p>簡單名稱：</p><blockquote><strong>角色方向不能隨意交換</strong></blockquote><p>最重要的問題：</p><blockquote><strong>誰對誰做了什麼？</strong></blockquote><p>再檢查：</p><blockquote><strong>如果兩個角色交換，原來的關係還能保持嗎？</strong></blockquote><p>有時答案是「不能」。</p><p>例如：</p><blockquote>Anna is older than Lucy.</blockquote><blockquote>（Anna 比 Lucy 年長。）</blockquote><p>角色交換後需要變成：</p>","<blockquote>Lucy is younger than Anna.</blockquote><blockquote>（Lucy 比 Anna 年輕。）</blockquote><p>有時答案是「目前不知道」。</p><p>例如：</p><blockquote>Peter calls Mary.</blockquote><blockquote>（Peter 打電話給 Mary。）</blockquote><p>Mary 有沒有打電話給 Peter，仍然需要新的資訊。</p><p>也有少數關係可以交換：</p><blockquote>next to （在……旁邊） sisters （姊妹）</blockquote><p>因此，判斷的核心不只是看兩個名字和一個動詞，更要保留：</p><blockquote><strong>角色、方向、關係詞。</strong></blockquote>"]}]}});
